#X text 82 626 0: messages (see Messages below), f 64;
#X obj 60 670 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 694 0: signal left \; 1: signal right \; 2: events: value \, dump, f 64;
#X obj 60 770 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 794 <pitch> <velocity> \, note <p> <v>: note on/off (0 = off) \; <p> <v> <channel>: from [notein] \, filtered by ch1 \; <control> <0-127>: set a control by name \, e.g. har1 64 \; ctl <index> <0-127> \, params v0 v1 ...: set by index \; <setting> <value>: e.g. mode 1 (see Settings below) \; bend <-1..1>: pitch bend of all voices (master clock) \; defaults \, reset: default values \, reset also stops all voices \; panic: all voices off \; get <name>: reply 'value <name> <v>' on outlet 2 \; print: voices \, values and sample rate to the Pd window \; dump: send all values to outlet 2 as 'dump pdoly8 v0 ..' \; dump pdoly8 v0 v1 ...: restore such a dump (this voice only) \; voice <i> <p> \, voiceoff <i>: play one voice directly, f 64;
#X obj 60 1030 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ (index\ name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1054 0 wav1 (127) Waveform of DCO1: 0 = square net (feet about \; 1:1:1:1) \, 127 = saw net (1:1/2:1/4:1/8 \, a step wave \, 16' +8 \; dB). Weights measured on a Poly-800\; continuous in between. \; 1 wav2 (127) Waveform of DCO2 \, same range. \; 2 har1 (64) Foot combination of DCO1. 15 original combinations \; at 0 \, 9 \, 18 ... 127 \, from one to the next a single foot fades \; in or out: 16' alone \, all feet at 64 \, 2' alone. \; 3 har2 (64) Foot combination of DCO2 \, same path. \; 4 intv (0) Interval of DCO2 above DCO1 \, 0-12 semitones. \; 5 detn (0) Detune of DCO2 \, 0 to -20 cents (the original's 4 \; steps lie at 0 \, 42 \, 85 \, 127). \; 6 lev1 (127) Level of DCO1. \; 7 lev2 (0) Level of DCO2 (DOUBLE only). Above full scale (lev1 \; + lev2 > 127) both are scaled down together., f 64;
#X obj 60 1306 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Settings\ (name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1330 mode (2) 1 = WHOLE: one DCO per voice \, 2 = DOUBLE: two DCOs \; oct1 \, oct2 (0) octave of DCO1 / DCO2 -1 \, 0 \, 1 \; nois (0) white noise level 0-15 \, sounds while a voice sounds \; sprd (0.5) stereo spread of the 4 voices 0-1 \; levl (0.5) output level 0-2 \; mrph (8) smoothing of wav \, har and lev changes in ms \; hold (1) released voices keep sounding until the next phrase \; a4 (440) tuning in Hz \; tune (0) master tune +-50 cents \; bnd (2) pitch bend range in semitones (original: up to 7) \; mgf (5) vibrato rate in Hz \; mgi (0) vibrato depth in cents (triangle on the master clock) \; hsnp (1) plateau around each foot combination \, in har steps \; ch1 (0) MIDI channel for p v ch lists \, 0 = any \; tone (1) 1: output response measured on a Poly-800 with the \; VCF fully open (54 Hz high-pass \, 2 poles at 7.5 kHz) \, 0: off, f 64;
#X obj 60 1614 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty How\ the\ Poly-800\ makes\ its\ sound 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1638 One master clock feeds the MSM5232: 8 tone generators in two \; groups (TG0-3 = DCO1 \, TG4-7 = DCO2). Each key becomes an \; integer divider from the chip's ROM \, then a binary counter \; whose bits are the 16' \, 8' \, 4' and 2' squares \, locked in \; phase. The four feet of a group are summed to a square or a \; step saw. Tune \, bend and vibrato move the master clock \, so \; all voices move together. Detune thins out DCO2's clock. \; Every edge is band-limited: analog edges \, no aliasing., f 64;
#X obj 60 1794 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Foot\ path\ (har) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1818 0: 16' / 9: 16'8' / 18: 16'8'4' / 27: 16'4' / 36: 16'4'2' \; 45: 16'2' / 54: 16'8'2' / 64: all feet / 73: 8'4'2' \; 82: 8'2' / 91: 8' / 100: 8'4' / 109: 4' / 118: 4'2' / 127: 2' \; On these values the sound is exactly the original. In \; between one foot fades \, so har can be modulated smoothly., f 64;
#X obj 60 1926 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Envelopes 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1950 pdoly8~ has no envelopes and no filter yet. A key gates its \; voice with a short de-click ramp\; shape the level with an \; external VCA. With hold 1 a released chord keeps sounding \; until the next phrase. The chip's counters run freely \, so \; a note-on does not restart the phase (as on the original)., f 64;
#X obj 60 2058 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets\ and\ steps 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2082 Per-step values: connect the voice to [skpreset name] \; (outlet 2 -> inlet 0 \, outlet 0 -> voice inlet). A slot \; number 0-15 then recalls and keeps the values for a step. \; More in skpreset-help.pd (click to open)., f 64;
#X msg 82 2156 dir;
#X obj 82 2182 pdcontrol;
#X obj 82 2208 list prepend skpreset-help.pd;
#X msg 82 2234 \; pd open \$1 \$2;
#X text 132 2156 <- click to open skpreset-help.pd, f 40;
